 editorial migration from the legacy category; unrepresented facets remain unassessed.","tree:evidenceAssessment":[{"@id":"urn:uuid:7d0547f2-6239-5a56-82a3-1c846701c866#assessment-node%3Afreeenergy%3Adevelopment"},{"@id":"urn:uuid:7d0547f2-6239-5a56-82a3-1c846701c866#assessment-node%3Afreeenergy%3AmapStatus"}],"tree:claimFingerprint":"9cf4521d"},{"@id":"urn:uuid:7d0547f2-6239-5a56-82a3-1c846701c866#node-gap_activeinf","@type":["schema:DefinedTerm","prov:Entity","tree:OpenResearchDirection"],"schema:identifier":"gap_activeinf","schema:name":"Active inference at scale","schema:description":"Research direction: test whether active-inference objectives can support competitive, large-scale agents. Existing work has not yet established parity with frontier-scale model-based agents.","schema:inDefinedTermSet":{"@id":"urn:uuid:7d0547f2-6239-5a56-82a3-1c846701c866"},"schema:url":{"@id":"./#node=gap_activeinf"},"schema:citation":[{"@id":"urn:uuid:7d0547f2-6239-5a56-82a3-1c846701c866#paper-arxiv-2006.04176"},{"@id":"urn:uuid:7d0547f2-6239-5a56-82a3-1c846701c866#paper-arxiv-2112.01871"}],"tree:recordType":"atlasEntry","tree:startYear":2026,"tree:endYear":2026,"tree:dateLabel":"2026","tree:lane":{"@id":"urn:uuid:7d0547f2-6239-5a56-82a3-1c846701c866#lane-roots"},"tree:legacyClassification":{"@id":"urn:uuid:7d0547f2-6239-5a56-82a3-1c846701c866#classification-g"},"tree:legacyClassificationCode":"g","tree:legacyClassificationLabel":"Open direction","tree:kind":"open_direction","tree:significance":"not_assessed","tree:activity":"not_assessed","tree:trajectory":"not_assessed","tree:statusAsOf":"2026-08-04","tree:statusConfidence":"low","tree:statusRationale":"Low-confidence editorial migration from the legacy category; unrepresented facets remain unassessed.","tree:evidenceAssessment":[{"@id":"urn:uuid:7d0547f2-6239-5a56-82a3-1c846701c866#assessment-node%3Agap_activeinf%3Adevelopment"},{"@id":"urn:uuid:7d0547f2-6239-5a56-82a3-1c846701c866#assessment-node%3Agap_activeinf%3AmapStatus"}],"tree:researchQuestion":["Can active-inference objectives produce compute-matched agents that equal strong model-based reinforcement-learning baselines on planning, adaptation, robustness, and efficiency?"],"tree:paperAssociation":[{"@id":"urn:uuid:7d0547f2-6239-5a56-82a3-1c846701c866#paper-link-gap_activeinf%3E2006.04176"},{"@id":"urn:uuid:7d0547f2-6239-5a56-82a3-1c846701c866#paper-link-gap_activeinf%3E2112.01871"}],"tree:claimFingerprint":"365cd761","tree:directionClaimState":"editorial_hypothesis","tree:directionAsOf":"2026-08-04","tree:directionConfidence":"high","tree:closureCriteria":"Under identical observations, model capacity, environment steps, and tuning budgets, an active-inference agent matches or exceeds strong model-based baselines across several environment families, with objective ablations identifying where expected-free-energy terms add value.","tree:partialResult":["Deep active inference with Monte Carlo tree search plans in dSprites and Animal-AI environments.","Discrete active-inference agents and the maintained pymdp library establish reproducible small-scale feasibility."],"tree:starterProject":["Individual: Implement a pymdp or neural active-inference agent on MiniGrid and compare it with PPO and a model-based baseline under fixed environment-step and tuning budgets.","Small lab: Run preregistered objective ablations across MiniGrid, Procgen, and selected DeepMind Control Suite tasks, measuring adaptation after dynamics and reward shifts.","Well-funded lab: Build a distributed active-inference agent and conduct a compute-matched simulation-to-robot evaluation with robustness, calibration, and wall-clock efficiency measurements."],"tree:counterexample":["Fountas et al. demonstrate a deep active-inference MCTS agent in continuous-state simulations.","Sajid et al. compare active inference with reinforcement learning in discrete Gym-style settings.","pymdp provides a maintained implementation for discrete Markov decision processes."],"tree:crowdedness":"Low to medium; active communities exist, but large compute-matched benchmark studies are uncommon.","tree:tractability":"High for controlled comparisons and medium for broad generalization or robotics.","tree:noveltyReview":{"@value":{"status":"targeted_search","checkedAt":"2026-08-04","scope":"arXiv titles and abstracts for active inference, expected free energy, robotics, planning, and reinforcement learning, plus modern control benchmarks and official implementations.","note":"Existing demonstrations are mainly small, simulated, or robotics-specific; the search did not establish priority or exhaust every venue."},"@type":"@json"},"tree:researchResources":{"@value":{"benchmarks":["MiniGrid","Procgen","DeepMind Control Suite","Animal-AI"],"code":["https://github.com/infer-actively/pymdp","https://github.com/zfountas/deep-active-inference-mc"],"datasets":["https://github.com/google-deepmind/dsprites-dataset","Procedurally generated interaction traces from MiniGrid, Procgen, and Animal-AI"],"estimated":{"individual":"1 x 24-48 GB GPU for several days","smallLab":"4-8 x 80 GB GPUs for 1-2 weeks","wellFundedLab":"32-64 accelerators for a multi-suite sweep and robotics follow-up"}},"@type":"@json"}},{"@id":"urn:uuid:7d0547f2-6239-5a56-82a3-1c846701c866#node-lt56","@type":["schema:DefinedTerm","prov:Entity","tree:ResearchDevelopment"],"schema:identifier":"lt56","schema:name":"Logic Theorist","schema:description":"Newell & Simon's first AI program — proved theorems from Principia by heuristic search over symbols. AI's opening move.","schema:inDefinedTermSet":{"@id":"urn:uuid:7d0547f2-6239-5a56-82a3-1c846701c866"},"schema:url":{"@id":"./#node=lt56"},"schema:citation":[{"@id":"urn:uuid:7d0547f2-6239-5a56-82a3-1c846701c866#work-newell-simon-logic-theory-1956"}],"tree:recordType":"atlasEntry","tree:startYear":1956,"tree:endYear":1956,"tree:dateLabel":"1956","tree:lane":{"@id":"urn:uuid:7d0547f2-6239-5a56-82a3-1c846701c866#lane-symbolic"},"tree:legacyClassification":