],"tree:researchQuestion":["Which simulation variations produce robust transfer rather than hiding reality gaps behind benchmark success?"],"tree:paperAssociation":[{"@id":"urn:uuid:7d0547f2-6239-5a56-82a3-1c846701c866#paper-link-simenv%3E1703.06907"}],"tree:claimFingerprint":"64d3cab1"},{"@id":"urn:uuid:7d0547f2-6239-5a56-82a3-1c846701c866#node-deeprlrobot","@type":["schema:DefinedTerm","prov:Entity","tree:ResearchDevelopment"],"schema:identifier":"deeprlrobot","schema:name":"Deep RL manipulation","schema:description":"Grasping via RL and domain randomization (OpenAI's Rubik's hand). Sample hunger stalled it; imitation + foundation models took the baton.","schema:inDefinedTermSet":{"@id":"urn:uuid:7d0547f2-6239-5a56-82a3-1c846701c866"},"schema:url":{"@id":"./#node=deeprlrobot"},"tree:recordType":"atlasEntry","tree:startYear":2017,"tree:endYear":2017,"tree:dateLabel":"2017","tree:lane":{"@id":"urn:uuid:7d0547f2-6239-5a56-82a3-1c846701c866#lane-robotics"},"tree:legacyClassification":{"@id":"urn:uuid:7d0547f2-6239-5a56-82a3-1c846701c866#classification-d"},"tree:legacyClassificationCode":"d","tree:legacyClassificationLabel":"Dormant","tree:kind":"development","tree:significance":"not_assessed","tree:activity":"dormant","tree:trajectory":"not_assessed","tree:statusAsOf":"2026-08-04","tree:statusConfidence":"low","tree:statusRationale":"Low-confidence editorial migration from the legacy category; unrepresented facets remain unassessed.","tree:evidenceAssessment":[{"@id":"urn:uuid:7d0547f2-6239-5a56-82a3-1c846701c866#assessment-node%3Adeeprlrobot%3Adevelopment"},{"@id":"urn:uuid:7d0547f2-6239-5a56-82a3-1c846701c866#assessment-node%3Adeeprlrobot%3AmapStatus"}],"tree:claimFingerprint":"a35adfa2"},{"@id":"urn:uuid:7d0547f2-6239-5a56-82a3-1c846701c866#node-selfdriving","@type":["schema:DefinedTerm","prov:Entity","tree:ResearchDevelopment"],"schema:identifier":"selfdriving","schema:name":"Self-driving's long grind","schema:description":"A decade of overpromise, then real robotaxis at scale (Waymo, 2024–26). The long tail was the whole problem — and it's yielding slowly.","schema:inDefinedTermSet":{"@id":"urn:uuid:7d0547f2-6239-5a56-82a3-1c846701c866"},"schema:url":{"@id":"./#node=selfdriving"},"tree:recordType":"atlasEntry","tree:startYear":2018,"tree:endYear":2018,"tree:dateLabel":"2018","tree:lane":{"@id":"urn:uuid:7d0547f2-6239-5a56-82a3-1c846701c866#lane-robotics"},"tree:legacyClassification":{"@id":"urn:uuid:7d0547f2-6239-5a56-82a3-1c846701c866#classification-a"},"tree:legacyClassificationCode":"a","tree:legacyClassificationLabel":"Active","tree:kind":"development","tree:significance":"not_assessed","tree:activity":"active","tree:trajectory":"not_assessed","tree:statusAsOf":"2026-08-04","tree:statusConfidence":"low","tree:statusRationale":"Low-confidence editorial migration from the legacy category; unrepresented facets remain unassessed.","tree:evidenceAssessment":[{"@id":"urn:uuid:7d0547f2-6239-5a56-82a3-1c846701c866#assessment-node%3Aselfdriving%3Adevelopment"},{"@id":"urn:uuid:7d0547f2-6239-5a56-82a3-1c846701c866#assessment-node%3Aselfdriving%3AmapStatus"}],"tree:claimFingerprint":"1dc44232"},{"@id":"urn:uuid:7d0547f2-6239-5a56-82a3-1c846701c866#node-rtfm","@type":["schema:DefinedTerm","prov:Entity","tree:ResearchDevelopment"],"schema:identifier":"rtfm","schema:name":"Robot foundation models","schema:description":"SayCan and RT-1 began the language-grounded lineage; RT-2, Open X-Embodiment, OpenVLA and π0 scaled vision-language-action learning. Robotics' claimed 'GPT moment' is still being tested.","schema:inDefinedTermSet":{"@id":"urn:uuid:7d0547f2-6239-5a56-82a3-1c846701c866"},"schema:url":{"@id":"./#node=rtfm"},"schema:citation":[{"@id":"urn:uuid:7d0547f2-6239-5a56-82a3-1c846701c866#paper-arxiv-2204.01691"},{"@id":"urn:uuid:7d0547f2-6239-5a56-82a3-1c846701c866#paper-arxiv-2212.06817"},{"@id":"urn:uuid:7d0547f2-6239-5a56-82a3-1c846701c866#paper-arxiv-2307.15818"},{"@id":"urn:uuid:7d0547f2-6239-5a56-82a3-1c846701c866#paper-arxiv-2310.08864"},{"@id":"urn:uuid:7d0547f2-6239-5a56-82a3-1c846701c866#paper-arxiv-2406.09246"},{"@id":"urn:uuid:7d0547f2-6239-5a56-82a3-1c846701c866#paper-arxiv-2410.24164"}],"tree:recordType":"atlasEntry","tree:startYear":2022,"tree:endYear":2022,"tree:dateLabel":"2022","tree:lane":{"@id":"urn:uuid:7d0547f2-6239-5a56-82a3-1c846701c866#lane-robotics"},"tree:legacyClassification":{"@id":"urn:uuid:7d0547f2-6239-5a56-82a3-1c846701c866#classification-h"},"tree:legacyClassificationCode":"h","tree:legacyClassificationLabel":"Hot frontier","tree:kind":"development","tree:significance":"not_assessed","tree:activity":"high_activity","tree:trajectory":"not_assessed","tree:statusAsOf":"2026-08-04","tree:statusConfidence":"low","tree:statusRationale":"Low-confidence editorial migration from the legacy category; unrepresented facets remain unassessed.","tree:evidenceAssessment":[{"@id":"urn:uuid:7d0547f2-6239-5a56-82a3-1c846701c866#assessment-node%3Artfm%3Adevelopment"},{"@id":"urn:uuid:7d0547f2-6239-5a56-82a3-1c846701c866#assessment-node%3Artfm%3AmapStatus"}],"tree:researchTier":"integrated","tree:tag":["robotics","foundation models","multimodal"],"tree:researchQuestion":["Which forms of internet-scale pretraining transfer to safe, data-efficient physical generalization?"],"tree:paperAssociation":[{"@id":"urn:uuid:7d0547f2-6239-5a56-82a3-1c846701c866#paper-link-rtfm%3E2204.01691"},{"@id":"urn:uuid:7d0547f2-6239-5a56-82a3-1c846701c866#paper-link-rtfm%3E2212.06817"},{"@id":"urn:uuid:7d0547f2-6239-5a56-82a3-1c846701c866#paper-link-rtfm%3E2307.15818"},{"@id":"urn:uuid:7d0547f2-6239-5a56-82a3-1c846701c866#paper-link-rtfm%3E2310.08864"},{"@id":"urn:uuid:7d0547f2-6239-5a56-82a3-1c846701c866#paper-link-rtfm%3E2406.09246"},{"@id":"urn:uuid:7d0547f2-6239-5a56-82a3-1c846701c866#paper-link-rtfm%3E2410.24164"}],"tree:claimFingerprint":"5b6c18c8"},{"@id":"urn:uuid:7d0547f2-6239-5a56-82a3-1c846701c866#node-humanoid26","@type":["schema:DefinedTerm","prov:Entity","tree:ResearchDevelopment"],"schema:identifier":"humanoid26","schema:name":"Humanoid renaissance","schema:description":"Optimus, Figure Helix, Unitree: billions chasing general-purpose bodies, first pilot deployments 2025–26. Hype versus unit economics, unresolved.","schema:inDefinedTermSet":{"@id":"urn:uuid:7d0547f2-6239-5a56-82a3-1c846701c866"},"schema:url":{"@id":"./#node=humanoid26"},"tree:recordType":"atlasEntry","tree:startYear":2024,"tree:endYear":2024,"tree:dateLabel":"2024","tree:lane":{"@id":"urn:uuid:7d0547f2-6239-5a56-82a3-1c846701c866#lane-robotics"},"tree:legacyClassification":{"@id":"urn:uuid:7d0547f2-6239-5a56-82a3-1c846701c866#classification-h"},"tree:legacyClassificationCode":"h","tree:legacyClassificationLabel":"Hot frontier","tree:kind":"development","tree:significance":"not_assessed","tree:activity":"high_activity","tree:trajectory":"not_assessed","tree:statusAsOf":"2026-08-04","tree:statusConfidence":"low","tree:statusRationale":"Low-confidence editorial migration from the legacy category; unrepresented facets remain unassessed.","tree:evidenceAssessment":[{"@id":"urn:uuid:7d0547f2-6239-5a56-82a3-1c846701c866#assessment-node%3Ahumanoid26%3Adevelopment"},{"@id":"urn:uuid:7d0547f2-6239-5a56-82a3-1c846701c866#assessment-node%3Ahumanoid26%3AmapStatus"}],"tree:claimFingerprint":"85f6107b"},{"@id":"urn:uuid:7d0547f2-6239-5a56-82a3-1c846701c866#node-gap_swarm","@type":["schema:DefinedTerm","prov:Entity","tree:OpenResearchDirection"],"schema:identifier":"gap_swarm","schema:name":"Swarms × foundation models","schema:description":"Research direction: scale foundation-model multi-robot systems to decentralized, online-adaptive and fault-tolerant swarms. Early systems already combine large models with multi-robot coordination; robust embodied scaling remains unresolved.","schema:inDefinedTermSet":{"@id":"urn:uuid:7d0547f2-6239-5a56-82a3-1c846701c866"},"schema:url":{"@id":"./#node=gap_swarm"},"schema:citation":[{"@id":"urn:uuid:7d0547f2-6239-5a56-82a3-1c846701c866#paper-arxiv-2509.14380"},{"@id":"urn:uuid:7d0547f2-6239-5a56-82a3-1c846701c866#paper-arxiv-2508.08574"}],"tree:recordType":"atlasEntry","tree:startYear":2026,"tree:endYear":2026,"tree:dateLabel":"2026","tree:lane":{"@id":"urn:uuid:7d0547f2-6239-5a56-82a3-1c846701c866#lane-robotics"},"tree:legacyClassification":{"@id":"urn:uuid:7d0547f2-6239-5a56-82a3-1c846701c866#classification-g"},"tree:legacyClassificationCode":"g","tree:legacyClassificationLabel":"Open direction","tree:kind":"open_direction","tree:significance":"not_assessed","tree:activity":"not_assessed","tree:trajectory":"not_assessed","tree:statusAsOf":"2026-08-04","tree:statusConfidence":"low","tree:statusRationale":"Low-confidence editorial migration from the legacy category; unrepresented facets remain unassessed.","tree:evidenceAssessment":[{"@id":"urn:uuid:7d0547f2-6239-5a56-82a3-1c846701c866#assessment-node%3Agap_swarm%3Adevelopment"},{"@id":"urn:uuid:7d0547f2-6239-5a56-82a3-1c846701c866#assessment-node%3Agap_swarm%3AmapStatus"}],"tree:researchQuestion":["Can foundation models improve embodied swarms while preserving decentralized execution, scaling to many inexpensive agents, and degrading gracefully under communication, member, sensor, and model failures?"],"tree:paperAssociation":[{"@id":"urn:uuid:7d0547f2-6239-5a56-82a3-1c846701c866#paper-link-gap_swarm%3E2509.14380"},{"@id":"urn:uuid:7d0547f2-6239-5a56-82a3-1c846701c866#paper-link-gap_swarm%3E2508.08574"}],"tree:claimFingerprint":"048b70b9","tree:directionClaimState":"editorial_hypothesis","tree:directionAsOf":"2026-08-04","tree:directionConfidence":"medium","tree:closureCriteria":"Show increasing team utility across at least three swarm sizes; keep execution decentralized with explicit per-agent compute and bandwidth caps; compare against strong modular decentralized baselines; test packet loss, partitions, Byzantine or faulty members, sensor corruption, and model failure; and transfer to a physical swarm.","tree:partialResult":["CRAFT uses language and vision-language foundation models to coach reinforcement learning for multi-robot coordination, and DeepFleet trains multi-agent foundation models on warehouse fleet movement data. RoCo and SMART-LLM coordinate smaller robot teams with language models. These invalidate a claim that the combination is nearly untouched, while leaving scalable online decentralized swarm intelligence and fault tolerance unresolved."],"tree:starterProject":["Individual: In ARGoS or Crazyswarm2 simulation, compare a local foundation-model coach with a modular decentralized controller across swarm sizes and a fixed packet-loss, sensor-noise, and member-dropout matrix.","Small lab: Test six to twelve inexpensive robots under packet loss, partitions, robot dropout, and stale or adversarial guidance; include centralization and communication-budget ablations.","Well-funded lab: Run a 50-plus heterogeneous-robot, multi-site study of online shared learning with decentralized execution, predefined graceful-degradation curves, safety supervision, and independent robustness auditing."],"tree:counterexample":["CRAFT trains coordinated multi-quadruped navigation and bimanual manipulation policies with foundation-model coaching and reports physical-policy transfer, but it is not a large, cheap, online-adaptive swarm under broad failures.","DeepFleet models warehouse fleets using data from hundreds of thousands of operational robots and robot-centric local graphs, but focuses on prediction and fleet design using proprietary operational data rather than general online swarm control.","RoCoBench and SMART-LLM show language-model planning for small multi-robot teams; scale, decentralization, latency, and graceful degradation remain limited."],"tree:crowdedness":"Medium for language-model multi-robot planning; low-medium for decentralized foundation-model swarms with systematic fault tolerance.","tree:tractability":"High in simulation, medium for a small physical fleet, and low for large heterogeneous swarms with convincing safety and robustness.","tree:noveltyReview":{"@value":{"status":"targeted_search","checkedAt":"2026-08-04","scope":"Targeted arXiv searches for foundation models in multi-robot coordination, fleet foundation models, LLM robot collaboration, decentralized swarm learning, embodied swarms, communication failures, and 2025-2026 follow-on papers; reference chaining from CRAFT, DeepFleet, RoCo, and SMART-LLM.","note":"Medium confidence that scalable, online, decentralized and fault-tolerant foundation-model swarms remain open. CRAFT and DeepFleet already demonstrate large-model coordination in smaller robot teams, narrowing the unresolved target. No priority claim is made."},"@type":"@json"},"tree:researchResources":{"@value":{"benchmarks":["RoCoBench","Multi-Agent Quadruped Environment tasks","Crazyswarm2 or ARGoS with a standardized communication-and-fault suite"],"code":["https://github.com/MandiZhao/robot-collab","https://github.com/SMARTlab-Purdue/SMART-LLM","https://github.com/IMRCLab/crazyswarm2","https://github.com/ilpincy/argos3"],"datasets":["RoCoBench language, plan, and trajectory tasks","SMART-LLM task data","A new open, fault-annotated multi-robot trajectory corpus; no canonical open foundation-model swarm corpus was identified"],"estimated":{"individual":"One modern GPU plus 16-64 CPU cores for simulation.","smallLab":"Four to twelve low-cost ground robots or three to six drones, four to eight GPUs, localization, spares, and safety supervision.","wellFundedLab":"Thirty-two to one hundred robots, mixed embodiments, motion capture or UWB localization, wireless instrumentation, safety operators, and substantial model-training compute."}},"@type":"@json"}},{"@id":"urn:uuid:7d0547f2-6239-5a56-82a3-1c846701c866#node-asimov","@type":["schema:DefinedTerm","prov:Entity","tree:ResearchDevelopment"],"schema:identifier":"asimov","schema:name":"Asimov's Three Laws","schema:description":"Fiction framed machine ethics decades before engineering could. Set the cultural frame every real safety debate still argues with.","schema:inDefinedTermSet":{"@id":"urn:uuid:7d0547f2-6239-5a56-82a3-1c846701c866"},"schema:url":{"@id":"./#node=asimov"},"schema:citation":[{"@id":"urn:uuid:7d0547f2-6239-5a56-82a3-1c846701c866#work-asimov-i-robot-1950"}],"tree:recordType":"atlasEntry","tree:startYear":1942,"tree:endYear":1942,"tree:dateLabel":"1942","tree:lane":{"@id":"urn:uuid:7d0547f2-6239-5a56-82a3-1c846701c866#lane-safety"},"tree:legacyClassification":{"@id":"urn:uuid:7d0547f2-6239-5a56-82a3-1c846701c866#classification-f"},"tree:legacyClassificationCode":"f","tree:legacyClassificationLabel":"Foundational","tree:kind":"development","tree:significance":"foundational","tree:activity":"not_assessed","tree:trajectory":"not_assessed","tree:statusAsOf":"2026-08-04","tree:statusConfidence":"low","tree:statusRationale":"Low-confidence editorial migration from the legacy category; unrepresented facets remain unassessed.","tree:evidenceAssessment":[{"@id":"urn:uuid:7d0547f2-6239-5a56-82a3-1c846701c866#assessment-node%3Aasimov%3Adevelopment"},{"@id":"urn:uuid:7d0547f2-6239-5a56-82a3-1c846701c866#assessment-node%3Aasimov%3AmapStatus"}],"tree:landmarkWorkAssociation":[{"@id":"urn:uuid:7d0547f2-6239-5a56-82a3-1c846701c866#work-link-asimov%3Easimov-i-robot-1950"}],"tree:claimFingerprint":"6ee7c5cf"},{"@id":"urn:uuid:7d0547f2-6239-5a56-82a3-1c846701c866#node-wienerwarn","@type":["schema:DefinedTerm","prov:Entity","tree:ResearchDevelopment"],"schema:identifier":"wienerwarn","schema:name":"Wiener's control warning","schema:description":"'If we use, to achieve our purposes, a mechanical agency with whose operation we cannot interfere…' — value misalignment stated plainly, in 1960.","schema:inDefinedTermSet":{"@id":"urn:uuid:7d0547f2-6239-5a56-82a3-1c846701c866"},"schema:url":{"@id":"./#node=wienerwarn"},"tree:recordType":"atlasEntry","tree:startYear":1960,"tree:endYear":1960,"tree:dateLabel":"1960","tree:lane":{"@id":"urn:uuid:7d0547f2-6239-5a56-82a3-1c846701c866#lane-safety"},"tree:legacyClassification":{"@id":"urn:uuid:7d0547f2-6239-5a56-82a3-1c846701c866#classification-f"},"tree:legacyClassificationCode":"f","tree:legacyClassificationLabel":"Foundational","tree:kind":"development","tree:significance":"foundational","tree:activity":"not_assessed","tree:trajectory":"not_assessed","tree:statusAsOf":"2026-08-04","tree:statusConfidence":"low","tree:statusRationale":"Low-confidence editorial migration from the legacy category; unrepresented facets remain unassessed.","tree:evidenceAssessment":[{"@id":"urn:uuid:7d0547f2-6239-5a56-82a3-1c846701c866#assessment-node%3Awienerwarn%3Adevelopment"},{"@id":"urn:uuid:7d0547f2-6239-5a56-82a3-1c846701c866#assessment-node%3Awienerwarn%3AmapStatus"}],"tree:claimFingerprint":"926b0d42"},{"@id":"urn:uuid:7d0547f2-6239-5a56-82a3-1c846701c866#node-weizenbaum","@type":["schema:DefinedTerm","prov:Entity","tree:ResearchDevelopment"],"schema:identifier":"weizenbaum","schema:name":"'Computer Power and Human Reason'","schema:description":"ELIZA's own creator warned against delegating judgment to machines. AI criticism as a serious intellectual tradition begins here.","schema:inDefinedTermSet":{"@id":"urn:uuid:7d0547f2-6239-5a56-82a3-1c846701c866"},"schema:url":{"@id":"./#node=weizenbaum"},"tree:recordType":"atlasEntry","tree:startYear":1976,"tree:endYear":1976,"tree:dateLabel":"1976","tree:lane":{"@id":"urn:uuid:7d0547f2-6239-5a56-82a3-1c846701c866#lane-safety"},"tree:legacyClassification":{"@id":"urn:uuid:7d0547f2-6239-5a56-82a3-1c846701c866#classification-f"},"tree:legacyClassificationCode":"f","tree:legacyClassificationLabel":"Foundational","tree:kind":"development","tree:significance":"foundational","tree:activity":"not_assessed","tree:trajectory":"not_assessed","tree:statusAsOf":"2026-08-04","tree:statusConfidence":"low","tree:statusRationale":"Low-confidence editorial migration from the legacy category; unrepresented facets remain unassessed.","tree:evidenceAssessment":[{"@id":"urn:uuid:7d0547f2-